{
  "summary": "This review examines thermal management materials for electronic devices across device and package levels. It analyzes thermal transport mechanisms, material properties, and interface effects to identify bottlenecks in heat dissipation pathways. The study emphasizes that intrinsic thermal conductivity alone is insufficient; dimensions, processing, and interfaces critically influence thermal performance. Key bottlenecks and material requirements for high-power-density devices are defined.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Intrinsic thermal conductivity alone cannot determine thermal performance due to dimensional, processing, and interface effects",
    "Device-level materials (semiconductors, metals, dielectrics) and thermal interface materials (TIMs) are critical for heat dissipation",
    "Key bottlenecks in internal heat-dissipation pathways define material and interface requirements for high-power-density electronic devices"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes that thermal performance in high-power-density electronics depends on integrated material properties, interface engineering, and dimensional considerations beyond intrinsic thermal conductivity."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines cardio-immune interactions in novel radioimmunotherapy, particularly for thoracic cancers. It analyzes how tumor radiosensitization mechanisms like cGAS-STING signaling and myeloid remodeling may concurrently affect cardiac immune homeostasis. The study identifies radiation parameters (dose rate, distribution) as critical modulators of this balance and highlights a translational gap in cardiac immune profiling for emerging modalities. It proposes a tumor-blood-heart framework for risk stratification, emphasizing the need for prospective validation to optimize therapy safety and efficacy.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Tumor radiosensitization pathways (e.g., cGAS-STING) may disrupt cardiac immune homeostasis",
    "Radiation parameters significantly influence the tumor-cardiac immune balance",
    "Direct cardiac immune profiling remains limited for emerging radiotherapy modalities"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cardio-immone immune crosstalk as a critical determinant in optimizing radioimmunotherapy safety and efficacy, advancing the understanding of tissue-specific immune responses during radiation treatment."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether brief dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a transient high-fat diet (HFD) exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates inflammation to levels seen in chronic obesity. HFD outside this window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the window reduces disease severity. Mechanistically, HFD rapidly recruits neutrophils, which express Nlrp3 and Il1b, driving pathogenic TH17 cell activation. Post-recovery, a chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cell population persists, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent low-fat diet. These findings demonstrate that short-term dietary states during inflammation can durably reprogram immune responses.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates skin inflammation to chronic obesity levels",
    "HFD outside this window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the window blunts disease amplification",
    "Neutrophil-mediated Nlrp3-Il1b axis licenses pathogenic TH17 cells, with persistent tissue-resident memory T cells after recovery"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that transient dietary states during acute inflammation can durably reprogram immune memory, revealing a critical temporal window for dietary interventions to modulate inflammatory disease trajectories."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing all-solid-state lithium-selenium batteries by engineering submolecular selenium species. The researchers converted crystalline cyclo-Se8 into amorphous Sex (x < 4) anchored on graphene, improving electronic conductivity and lithium diffusion. A Li2O-nanoshell-modified sulfide electrolyte stabilized interfaces. Batteries achieved 86% capacity retention after 2800 cycles at 3 C under 8 MPa and 420 Wh kg-1 energy density at 2.5 MPa, with recyclable selenium species post-cycling.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Submolecular Sex cathodes (x < 4) anchored on graphene increased electronic conductivity to 13 S cm-1",
    "Li2O-nanoshell-modified sulfide electrolyte stabilized interfaces with Li metal and Se cathode",
    "All-solid-state Li-Se batteries retained 86% capacity after 2800 cycles at 3 C under 8 MPa"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes submolecular chalcogen chemistry as a design strategy for low-pressure, recyclable, high-energy all-solid-state batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This review evaluates long-term immunological, oncological, and clinical outcomes after adult thymectomy by integrating molecular mechanisms and real-world evidence. It addresses historical misconceptions about the thymus as immunologically redundant, noting recent studies showing increased mortality and cancer risk post-surgery. The analysis highlights functional thymus activity in exporting naïve T cells and thymulin, emphasizing the need to distinguish incidental versus therapeutic resection to avoid iatrogenic immunosenescence while reducing cancer risk in specific conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Adult thymectomy increases 5-year all-cause mortality and cancer risk in some populations",
    "The thymus continues to export naïve T cells and produce thymulin for immune regulation",
    "Partial thymectomy may preserve immunocompetence in oncologically feasible cases"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This synthesis clarifies the functional role of the adult th:ymus in immune maintenance and provides critical context for clinical decision-making regarding thymectomy indications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates achieving reversible photo-charging in photo-rechargeable batteries using stacked 1T/2H MoS2 bifunctional cathodes. The researchers integrated photo-active 2H and energy-storage 1T MoS2 phases with nickel oxide to enhance conductivity and phase stability. An external resistance was used to balance self-discharge and photo-charging currents. The system demonstrated reversible photo-charging for over ten cycles with a 100% photo-charging capacity ratio within two hours of illumination, achieving 110.55 mAh g- 1 specific capacity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Reversible photo-charging for over ten cycles using stacked 1T/2H MoS2 cathodes",
    "100% photo-charging capacity ratio achieved within 2 hours of illumination",
    "110.55 mAh g-1 specific capacity with zinc deposition at the anode"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a method for genuine, reversible photo-charging in batteries without side reactions, advancing sustainable energy storage systems that directly convert solar energy into stored electrical energy."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated HPV-positive oral squamous cell carcinoma (OSCC) by correlating clinical parameters with immune and molecular markers. Retrospective analysis revealed significant differences in tumor site, differentiation, and 5-year survival between HPV-positive and negative OSCC. IHC showed downregulated p53 and Cyclin D1 in HPV-positive tumors, while MDSCs increased progressively from precancerous lesions to OSCC, and Tregs were elevated in OSCC patients. Transcriptomic analysis identified circRNA-miRNA axes targeting Calsequestrin 2 (CASQ2), suggesting immunosuppressive remodeling and a core pathogenic mechanism for HPV-positive OSCC progression.",
  "key_findings": [
    "HPV-positive OSCC patients exhibited significant differences in tumor site, pathological differentiation, and 5-year survival compared to HPV-negative OSCC",
    "HPV-positive OSCC tissues showed downregulated p53 and Cyclin D1 protein expression",
    "Two circRNA-miRNA regulatory axes specifically target Calsequestrin 2 (CASQ2) in HPV-positive OSCC"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies a novel circRNA-miRNA regulatory mechanism driving immunosuppressive remodeling in HPV-positive OSCC, providing a potential target for precision immunotherapy."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a bio-derived Janus membrane for selective aromatic recovery from saline industrial wastewaters. The membrane integrates a wood scaffold with a polydimethylsiloxane (PDMS) layer to enable soft-gated transport of aromatic compounds. Spectroscopic analyses confirm transient hydroxyl-mediated phenol capture and efficient diffusion through PD. It achieves 99.4% salt rejection and a phenol mass-transfer coefficient of 36.9 × 10-7 m s-1, with high tensile strength (∼70 MPa) and sustained performance in petrochemical and oilfield wastewaters. Life-cycle assessments show over 85% environmental impact reduction and annual CO2 mitigation of 42,000 tons.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The membrane achieves 99.4% salt rejection and a phenol mass-transfer coefficient of 36.9 × 10-7 m s-1",
    "It demonstrates sustained performance in petrochemical and offshore oilfield wastewaters with a tensile strength of ∼70 MPa",
    "Life-cycle analyses indicate over 85% reductions in environmental impact and annual CO2 mitigation of 42,000 tons"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This bio-derived Janus membrane architecture enables efficient aromatic recovery from saline wastewaters while minimizing environmental impact, advancing sustainable resource recovery from industrial effluents."
}

{
  "summary": "This study retrospectively analyzed clinical data from sepsis patients to evaluate the prognostic value of Treg cells, APTT, fibrinogen, and CRP. Using ROC curves and AUC calculations, the researchers found that combining these four markers improved mortality prediction accuracy (AUC 0.851) compared to individual markers (AUCs 0.779, 0.635, 0.756, 0.720). The results indicate these biomarkers collectively enhance sepsis prognosis assessment.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Combined Treg cells, APTT, fibrinogen, and CRP demonstrated an AUC of 0.851 for predicting sepsis mortality",
    "Individual markers showed AUCs ranging from 0.635 to 0.779 for mortality prediction",
    "The combination significantly outperformed single biomarkers in prognostic accuracy"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a multi-marker approach that enhances the predictive capability for sepsis mortality, providing a potential tool for improved clinical risk stratification in sepsis management."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the mechanical instability in low-pressure solid-state Na-S batteries with thick sulfur cathodes, where solid-solid contact loss impedes charge recovery. Researchers developed chemically reactivatable sulfide interfaces using Fe3C-MnO heteropoints in nitrogen-doped carbon nanotubes. The interface maintains electronic coupling and sulfide affinity, enabling sustained sulfur recovery under low pressure. At 0.2 MPa, a 200 µm cathode with 8.3 mg cm⁻² sulfur achieved 696 Wh kg⁻¹ energy density and stable cycling.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Fe3C-MnO heteropoints in nitrogen-doped carbon nanotubes create reactivatable sulfide interfaces",
    "The interface sustains sulfur recovery under low pressure (0.2 MPa) despite mechanical confinement",
    "A 200 µm cathode with 8.3 mg cm⁻² sulfur achieved 696 Wh kg⁻¹ energy density and stable cycling"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a strategy to decouple reversible sulfur chemistry from mechanical constraints in solid-state Na-S batteries, enabling high-energy storage with thick cathodes under low operational pressure."
}

{
  "summary": "This review investigates maternal thyroid status and its impact on immune adaptation at the maternal-fetal interface, distinguishing direct versus indirect pathways. It examines how thyroid hormones influence immune cells through placental transport, metabolism, and receptor signaling. Key findings include limited evidence for direct effects on uterine natural killer cells and decidual macrophages, context-dependent effects on trophoblast behavior, and the need for integrated approaches to clarify hormone-immune interactions in pregnancy.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Placental transport proteins (MCT8/MCT10 and DIO2/DIO3) regulate local thyroid hormone availability",
    "Human trophoblast and decidual studies show context-dependent effects on trophoblast invasion and decidualization",
    "Direct evidence for thyroid hormone effects on uter. NK cells and decidual macrophages is gestational-age dependent and limited"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review clarifies the complex interplay between maternal thyroid status and immune adaptation in pregnancy by distinguishing direct and indirect pathways, highlighting the need for integrated tissue-level analyses to resolve hormone-immune interactions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of dense tumor stroma limiting nanomedicine efficacy by engineering a Janus nanomotor integrating rhenium(I)-based molecular actuators with glucose oxidase. The nanomotor generates autonomous motility via asymmetric glucose consumption, enhancing intratumoral delivery. Upon light activation, it simultaneously produces reactive oxygen species for photodynamic therapy and induces membrane permeabilization through photoisomerization. In murine models, this approach achieved superior tumor suppression with robust antitumor immunity, including increased T cells and dendritic cell maturation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Engineered Re(I)-based molecular actuators enable autonomous nanomotor motility via glucose oxidase-catalyzed glucose consumption",
    "Light-activated dual functionality: ROS generation for photodynamic therapy and membrane permeabilization via E/Z photoisomerization",
    "Re1@N. Ms-mediated treatment induced ferroptosis/pyroptosis and enhanced antitumor immunity in murine tumors"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work pioneers the integration of a metal-complex-based molecular actuator with tumor-microenvironment-adaptive nanomotors, establishing a novel strategy to overcome stromal barriers and enhance combined photodynamic-photomechanical therapy efficacy."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how persistent inflammation leads to immune suppression, impairing host immunity and promoting cancer progression. It reviews mechanisms where inflammatory signals activate pathways like NF-κB and STAT3, recruiting immunosuppressive cells (MDSCs, TAMs, Tregs, Bregs, neutrophils) and causing T cell exhaustion. The research highlights interconnected pathways that facilitate tumor evasion of immune surveillance and suggests potential therapeutic targets for enhancing antitumor immunity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Persistent inflammation triggers immune-suppressive pathways via NF-κB and STAT3 signaling",
    "Inflammatory signals recruit and activate immunosuppressive cell types including MDSCs, TAMs, Tregs, Bregs, and neutrophils",
    "Chronic inflammation causes T cell exhaustion and immune checkpoint upregulation, hindering antitumor immunity"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review elucidates the mechanistic links between inflammation-induced immune suppression and cancer progression, providing a foundation for targeting immunosuppressive pathways to improve therapeutic responses in oncology."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates H. pylori's role in oral caries progression, revealing its retention within S. mutans biofilms and association with transcriptional remodeling that increases cariogenic potential. In vivo rat models showed H. pylori co-colonization exacerbates caries and dysbiosis. The researchers developed GPAM, a hydrogel that uses light and ultrasound to generate ROS, disrupt biofilms, inhibit H. pylori urease via Cu2+, and promote remineralization through ACP. This dual-responsive system offers a targeted therapeutic approach for H. pylori-associated caries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "H. pylori persists within S. mutans biofilms and induces transcriptional remodeling",
    "H. pylori co-colonization accelerates caries progression and oral dysbiosis in rats",
    "GPAM hydrogel disrupts mixed biofilms via ROS generation, inhibits H. pylori urease, and promotes remineralization"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides mechanistic insights into H. pylori's oral pathogenesis and demonstrates a dual-responsive hydrogel therapy for targeted disruption of H. pylori-S. mutans biofilms in caries progression."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines linked suppression in transplantation, distinguishing it from bystander suppression and infectious tolerance. It investigates how antigen-specific regulatory T cells control multivalent alloimmune responses through direct, indirect, or semi-direct allorecognition. Findings indicate regulation of one antigen restrains other linked antigens in grafts or via shared APCs, with mechanisms involving CTLA-4, adenosine, and spatial organization. Clinical validation remains limited.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Regulation of one antigen restrains responses to physically linked antigens within a graft",
    "Mechanisms include CTLA-:4-dependent B7 removal, adenosine generation, and APC spatial organization",
    "Relevant interactions are concentrated in grafts and draining lymph nodes, not peripheral blood"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This study clarifies the mechanistic boundaries of linked suppression, providing a framework for translating preclinical models into clinical strategies for transplantation immunomodulation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a method for synthesizing wafer-scale graphene with controlled layer numbers, crystallographic orientation, and stacking order using chemical vapor deposition on oxidized single-crystal copper wafers. The approach employs a Cu(111)-Cu2O(using a Cu(111)-Cu2O(111) heterogeneous catalytic substrate to achieve 2-inch single-crystalline graphene films with tunable layer counts (2–5). The technique enables deterministic spatial patterning of alternating Bernal and rhombohedral stacking in trilayer graphene, confirmed by near-field nano-optics and angle-resolved photoemission spectroscopy. The films demonstrate exceptional thickness uniformity, high crystallinity, and ultra-flat surfaces, addressing key challenges in scalable 2D material production.",
  "key_findings": [
    "2-inch single-crystalline graphene films with tunable layer numbers (2–5) grown via chemical vapor deposition on oxidized Cu wafers",
    "Deterministic spatial patterning of alternating Bernal and rhombohedral stacking in trilayer graphene",
    "Exceptional thickness uniformity, high crystallinity, and ultra-flat surfaces in wafer-scale films"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a unified growth strategy for layer-controlled graphene with programmable stacking order, advancing scalable production of 2D materials for quantum property studies and device applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines ginsenoside Rg3's role in solid tumor therapy by analyzing its impact on the tumor immune microenvironment. It evaluates preclinical and clinical evidence for Rg3 across lung, breast, liver cancers, and melanoma. The compound suppresses oncogenic pathways (STAT3, PI3K, NF-κB), reduces immunosuppressive cytokines, induces immunogenic cell death, and modulates immune cell functions including macrophage polarization, T-cell responses, NK-cell cytotoxicity, and Treg/MDSC suppression. Rg3 also regulates hypoxia signaling via HIF-1α/VEGF. Nanocarrier delivery systems are proposed to address pharmacokinetic challenges, though its immunotherapeutic efficacy requires further validation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Rg3 suppresses oncogenic signaling pathways (STAT3, PI3K, NF-κB) in solid tumors",
    "Rg3 reduces immunosuppressive cytokines (IL-6, IL-10, TGF-β) and chemokines while inducing immunogenic cell death",
    "Rg3 modulates immune cell functions including macrophage polarization, T-cell responses, NK-cell cytotoxicity, and Treg/MDSC suppression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This study provides mechanistic insights into ginsenoside Rg3's multifaceted modulation of the tumor immune microenvironment, highlighting potential strategies for enhancing cancer immunotherapy through targeted molecular and cellular interventions."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines dead cell-based carriers as safer alternatives to living cells for biomedical applications. It evaluates fabrication strategies and delivery characteristics of microalgae, yeasts, bacteria, and mammalian cells for treating bacterial pneumonia, inflammatory bowel disease, and cancer. The study highlights enhanced safety, stability, and retention of bioactive molecules while addressing platform-specific limitations and translational challenges like standardized manufacturing and regulatory pathways.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Dead cell carriers offer improved safety and stability compared to living cells",
    "Four carrier types (microalgae, ye:sts, bacteria, mammalian cells) show therapeutic potential for specific diseases",
    "Key translational challenges include standardized manufacturing and regulatory pathways"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes dead cell carriers as viable, safer delivery platforms with enhanced stability and retained bioactive molecules, advancing the field of biocompatible drug delivery systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This narrative review examines interleukin-6's role across the preeclampsia spectrum from implantation to postpartum cardiovascular disease. It analyzes IL-6's involvement in maternal-fetal immune maladaptation, decidual immune dynamics, regulatory T-cell/T-helper-17 interactions, defective placentation, and endothelial injury. The study highlights IL-6 as a biomarker, mediator, and potential therapeutic target, noting human data remain associative with confounding cardiometabolic risks, while clinical trials show IL-6 inhibition reduces inflammation without improving cardiovascular outcomes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL-6 serves as a biomarker, mediator, and potential therapeutic target in preeclampsia",
    "Human data on IL-6 are associative and confounded by shared cardiometabolic risk factors",
    "IL-6 ligand inhibition reduces inflammation but does not decrease cardiovascular events in clinical trials"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review clarifies IL-6's multifaceted role in preeclampsia pathogenesis and its persistent impact on postpartum cardiovascular health, emphasizing the need for targeted measurement and intervention strategies beyond current associative biomarker approaches."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates supramolecular silica nanosieves (suprasilica) for selectively separating aromatic hydrocarbons from cyclic aliphatics in hydrocarbon feedstocks. Using a self-assembly sol-gel approach, researchers integrated hexasila-ureido-trianglamine (Δ-Si6) into silica matrices to create Δ-SiNx sieves. The nanosieves demonstrated high selectivity for benzene over cyclohexane (23.5) and toluene over methylcyclohexane (6.3) in vapor sorption and dynamic column tests, retaining performance in liquid phases like naphtha and crude oil. Metadynamics simulations suggest kinetic selectivity mechanisms.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Suprasilica nanosieves achieve high selectivity for aromatics over cyclic aliphatics in hydrocarbon feedstocks",
    "Δ-SiNx sieves maintain selective separation performance in vapor, dynamic column, and liquid phases including crude oil",
    "Metadynamics simulations indicate kinetic selectivity mechanisms where aromatic hydrocarbons pass through macrocyclic apertures with lower barriers"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "These suprasilica nanosieves provide a scalable, energy-efficient separation strategy for hydrocarbon purification with benchmark selectivity, advancing molecularly selective hydrocarbon separation technologies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated montelukast's impact on experimental food allergy in mice. Using an ovalbumin-induced model, researchers assessed allergic responses, serum IgE, colonic eosinophils, Foxp3 expression, and epithelial adhesion proteins. Results showed reduced anaphylaxis scores and colonic eosinophil infiltration with montelukast, while Foxp3 protein levels increased without significant changes in Treg function or E-cadherin expression. The findings suggest montelukast attenuates intestinal allergic inflammation through eosinophil modulation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Montelukast reduced colonic eosinophilic infiltration in ovalbumin-sensitized mice",
    "Montelukast increased colonic Foxp3 protein expression without significant changes in Treg function",
    "Eosinophil infiltration and E-cadherin expression showed opposing associations with allergic symptom severity"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This study provides evidence that montelukast can mitigate intestinal allergic inflammation in experimental food allergy models by targeting eosinophilic responses, offering insights into potential therapeutic mechanisms for food allergy-related conditions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses uneven solvation and unstable interfaces in PVDF-based polymer electrolytes for solid-state lithium metal batteries. The researchers developed an anchored fluoro-shielded solvation strategy using polyanionic anchoring sites and fluorinated segments. This approach created homogeneous Li+ transport, robust LiF-rich SEI, and high performance: 1.26×10-3 S cm-1 conductivity, 0.69 Li+ transference number, 5.27 V oxidative stability, and 80.2% capacity retention after 2000 cycles in Li||LiNi0.8Co0.1Mn0.1O2 batteries at 4.5 V/5 C.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Homogeneous Li+ transport enabled by spatially distributed anion-rich solvation pathways",
    "Robust LiF-rich solid electrolyte interphase formation",
    "High ionic conductivity (1.26×10-3 S cm-1) and 80.2% capacity retention after 2000 cycles"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This molecular design strategy provides a pathway to enhance solvation stability and interfacial robustness in polymer electrolytes for high-voltage, high-rate solid-state lithium metal batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how PIKFYVE inhibition affects lysosomal, mitochondrial, and redox homeostasis in Th17-polarized CD4+ T cells. Using proteomics and apilimod, it found reduced IL-17+ cells and increased Foxp3+ regulatory T cells. Key changes include enhanced lysosomal trafficking, mitochondrial hyperpolarization with elevated ROS, and decreased ATP. These alterations correlate with reduced Th17 differentiation and increased Treg generation, with NAC partially rescuing Foxp3+ cell production.",
  "key_findings": [
    "PIKFYVE inhibition reduced IL-17+ cells and increased Foxp3+ regulatory T cell generation",
    "Enhanced lysosomal acidification and autophagy markers accompanied by mitochondrial hyperpolarization and elevated ROS",
    "N-acetylcysteine partially restored Foxp3+ cell production, indicating redox sensitivity in the regulatory shift"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work links lysosomal phosphoinositide signaling to mitochondrial redox dynamics in T cell differentiation, providing mechanistic insights into how PIKFYVE modulation can shift Th17 responses toward regulatory T cells."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing proton transport in MXene nanoribbons for efficient single-atom electrocatalysts. Researchers developed edge-closed nanoribbons with sub-10 nm confined channels using a stiffness-mediated strategy that modulates critical collapse pressure. The nanorusing exhibited higher proton transport rates and surface proton concentration compared to nanoscrolls and nanosheets, enabling low overpotential (23 mV) and a Tafel slope of 25 mV dec-1 for hydrogen evolution reactions with single-atom Pt catalysts.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Edge-closed MXene nanoribbons with sub-10 nm confined channels were synthesized via stiffness-mediated tube collapse",
    "Enhanced proton transport rates and surface proton concentration relative to nanoscrolls and nanosheets",
    "Single-atom Pt catalysts achieved low overpotential (23 mV) and Tafel slope of 25 mV dec-1 in hydrogen evolution reactions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that engineered sub-10 nm confined channels in edge-closed MXene nanoribbons significantly improve proton transport for single-atom electrocatalysis, advancing the design of high-performance hydrogen evolution reaction catalysts."
}
